  "captured_at": "2026-11-04",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "text": "Role-based access control in the Zscaler Admin Console allows you to configure granular permissions for administrators on the Zscaler service."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Creating a Role",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "To create a role:"
    },
    {
      "item": "From the navigation menu, go to Administration > Role Management > Role Management.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          32,
          46
        ],
        [
          49,
          64
        ],
        [
          67,
          82
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Create Role.",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          17
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "The Create Role page appears.",
      "depth": 0,
      "strong": [
        [
          4,
          15
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "On the Create Role page, select the permissions you would like to assign to the role. For each permission category, subcategory, and individual permission, you can grant the role one of the following access levels:",
      "depth": 0,
      "number": 3,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          18
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "No Access: Prevents admins from accessing the selected feature or page.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          9
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "View Only: Allows admins to view the selected feature or page, but does not allow them to make any changes to it.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          9
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Full Access: Grants admins the ability to both view and make changes to the selected feature or page.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          11
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Configuring a mix of different permissions within a category causes the drop-down permissions menu for that category to display Mixed. Some individual permissions can only be configured as either No Access and View Only or No Access and Full Access. The drop-down menu for each permission category and subcategory only contain options that are shared by all individual permissions. For example, if you can only select No Access or View Only for an individual permission, the category and subcategory containing that permission only display No Access and View Only,",
      "depth": 0,
      "strong": [
        [
          128,
          133
        ],
        [
          196,
          205
        ],
        [
          210,
          219
        ],
        [
          223,
          232
        ],
        [
          237,
          248
        ],
        [
          418,
          427
        ],
        [
          431,
          440
        ],
        [
          540,
          549
        ],
        [
          554,
          563
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Permissions can be configured for the following:",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Platform",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Configure permissions for the entire Platform category, which encompasses management of general settings and preferences for the Zscaler Admin Console, alerts, and audit logs, or any of the following subcategories and individual permissions:",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          37,
          45
        ]
      ]
    },
